WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.360
The end of the Q? Borg history rewritten?&nbsp;
“Picard” season 2 left plenty unanswered.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.120
One of the most anticipated "Star Trek" returns&nbsp;
since the Next Generation crew came back is actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:17.360
John de Lancie, who reprised the role of enigmatic&nbsp;
and omnipotent trickster Q. And when he arrived,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.280
we knew right away he wasn't the same.&nbsp;
More than just older, Q seemed darker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.720
more sinister, and with a bitter edge. Once&nbsp;
again, Q put Picard through a personal test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.960
getting him to fix a change in time and&nbsp;
learn a lesson about himself along the way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.320
While this mirrored episodes like&nbsp;
"Tapestry" and "All Good Things,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.760
something was different this time&nbsp;
around. This time, Q was dying.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.240
According to Q, he was slowly losing his&nbsp;
powers and nearing the end of his existence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.040
something he didn't think possible. In the season&nbsp;
finale, "Farewell," Q says he's finally ready to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.600
cease being. He uses the last ounce of his&nbsp;
power to send Picard and his crew home and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.320
bring Elnor back to life. But is this really&nbsp;
the end of Q, or does death among the Q mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.800
an end to the entire Q continuum? In "Star&nbsp;
Trek: Discovery," Starfleet claims that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:06.685
haven't had an encounter with the continuum in 600&nbsp;
years, leaving a gap that could still be filled.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:12.000
In a shocking last-minute twist, Trekkies got&nbsp;
the answers to two long-unresolved questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.720
when Wesley Crusher made a surprise appearance,&nbsp;
showing that he was no longer in Starfleet, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.760
was now a Traveler, just like the enigmatic alien&nbsp;
we met on "The Next Generation." Wesley confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.640
that he and others like him employ the likes of&nbsp;
Tallinn and the Original Series' Gary Seven as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.760
"supervisors" who monitor historical events and&nbsp;
ensure that the timeline plays out as it should.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.760
"You interfere with me, with what I have to&nbsp;
do down there, and you'll change history."

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.600
When Wesley arrives, he's in 2024. He visits&nbsp;
Adam Soong's daughter Kore, who he recruits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:46.160
to join him. With her father disgraced and her&nbsp;
life a lie, Kore takes Wesley up on the offer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.480
and the two beam away. Though one might suspect&nbsp;
that Wesley is enlisting her to be a Traveler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.840
it seems more likely that Kore was&nbsp;
recruited to be the next Supervisor.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.520
Could Kore be assigned a new&nbsp;
subject to monitor in 2024,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.680
or some other time period? Could we see Wesley&nbsp;
and Kore return in the kind of spin-off that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.240
Gary Seven was created for — a show about a&nbsp;
time traveling agent watching over important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.560
historical events? Producer Alex Kurtzman&nbsp;
has teased some upcoming mystery projects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.653
in the "Star Trek" universe, and this is one&nbsp;
that definitely seems like a possibility.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.720
Cristóbal "Chris" Rios was introduced&nbsp;
as a rogue captain in the first season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.960
of "Picard." He left Starfleet under shadowy&nbsp;
circumstances following a scandal and coverup,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:28.000
and went on to become an independent operator,&nbsp;
captaining the starship La Sirena. At the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.560
the first season, he returned to Starfleet. Now&nbsp;
commander of the USS Stargazer, Captain Rios is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:38.000
transported back in time to 2024 alongside&nbsp;
Picard, Raffi, Jurati, and Seven of Nine.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.200
Rios falls in love with a 21st century woman&nbsp;
named Teresa, a doctor and mother running a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.080
clinic in Los Angeles. In the 25th century, Guinan&nbsp;
confirms that Rios lived out his life there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.920
starting a medical supply company, but&nbsp;
is this really the end of Rios' story?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.520
If "Star Trek" has taught us anything,&nbsp;
surprise returns are the order of the day.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.160
We know that La Sirena is equipped with a series&nbsp;
of holograms that use Rios' image, so it's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.320
impossible that he could return somewhere down the&nbsp;
line as one of his holographic assistants. Rios&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.780
proved a popular character with fans, so there's&nbsp;
a good chance we haven't seen the last of him yet.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:14.000
Introduced in Season 4 of "Star Trek: Voyager,"&nbsp;
Seven of Nine has been on a journey from being a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.840
villainous robotic drone reliant on the&nbsp;
Borg hive mind, to becoming a strong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.680
independent person who has reclaimed&nbsp;
her humanity, in many small steps.

00:03:22.722 --> 00:03:24.510
"Is something wrong?"

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.053
"I am unaccustomed to this. Borg do not sit."

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.520
She expressed interest in joining Starfleet when&nbsp;
the Voyager crew returned to the Alpha Quadrant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:37.120
wanting to follow in Captain Janeway's&nbsp;
footsteps. In the second season of "Picard",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:41.520
we learned that her dreams of Federation service&nbsp;
had remained just that, as Starfleet rejected her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:46.000
application thanks to her Borg past. Though&nbsp;
fellow former drone Icheb was accepted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.760
spending her entire adult life as a&nbsp;
Borg made Starfleet wary of Seven.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.400
In the finale of "Picard" Season 2, when Seven&nbsp;
and the rest of Picard's team return to the 25th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.640
century, Picard gives her a field commission.&nbsp;
Reasoning that Seven has the most experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:02.480
with the Borg and is best suited to lead the rest&nbsp;
of the mission, Picard gives her the captain's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:07.680
chair. With the Jurati Queen and her unique Borg&nbsp;
collective now requesting Federation membership,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:12.560
combined with her field commission, could&nbsp;
Starfleet reconsider Seven's application?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.240
Actor Jeri Ryan has already made it clear that&nbsp;
she will appear in the series' third season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:19.280
and it's entirely possible she&nbsp;
could be a Starfleet officer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.790
or a Borg ambassador, when we see her next.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:25.680
During "The Next Generation," the relationship&nbsp;
between Guinan and Picard was something of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:29.920
mystery. Some of it was resolved in the two-part&nbsp;
episode "Time's Arrow," in which Picard traveled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.400
back to 19th century Earth and met Guinan. From&nbsp;
her perspective, it was their first meeting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:40.000
but all that changed in "Picard." Leaving from&nbsp;
an altered timeline, Picard meets Guinan in 2024,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.280
and for her, their encounter in the 1890s never&nbsp;
happened, because the future Picard left from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:50.400
in "Time's Arrow" no longer existed. It seemed&nbsp;
that now their first meeting occurred in 2024.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.800
"I'll see you in 500 years, Picard."

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:56.160
"And I'll see you in a few minutes."

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.840
But with their mission complete, and the&nbsp;
timeline from "Time's Arrow" now restored,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:06.320
it would seem they've met twice in the past — in&nbsp;
1893, and again in 2024. However, in that version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.520
of 2024 she said she'd never met him, so how&nbsp;
exactly does Guinan's memory of Picard work? Are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:16.320
we now in a timeline where they never met in the&nbsp;
19th century? Or is this another case of infinite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:20.861
fragmented timelines we're living through? Maybe&nbsp;
this is one question we shouldn't be asking.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:25.840
"Picard" Season 2 took the show's crew on a&nbsp;
mission to restore a timeline fractured by Q.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.560
An important event in the past had been changed&nbsp;
and all of time altered as a result. We learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:35.840
that it centered on Picard's ancestor Renée, an&nbsp;
astronaut who led a mission to Europa in 2024,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:40.960
where she discovered a unique organism. Without&nbsp;
her mission's success, all of time was rewritten,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.600
and the future twisted into a dark reality where&nbsp;
non-humans were subjugated by the Confederation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.720
and Picard himself waged a&nbsp;
violent war of oppression.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:52.720
But with this organism, new technologies would&nbsp;
apparently be developed that would reverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.840
all of the environmental damage on&nbsp;
Earth. The failure of the Europa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:58.560
Mission meant the continued&nbsp;
decimation of the environment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:02.480
but it's not made clear how that would have&nbsp;
led to a totalitarian world government in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:07.840
the 25th century. Nor does it explain why Adam&nbsp;
Soong would be known as an anti-alien tyrant.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:12.720
"A safe galaxy is a human galaxy."

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.560
However, in Adam Soong's time of 2024,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:21.200
first official contact with intelligent alien&nbsp;
life is still at least 40 years away. How did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:25.680
his conversations about the future with Jurati&nbsp;
and Q lead him to take such an aggressive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:30.940
anti-alien stance, and why was it embraced&nbsp;
before humanity had met any aliens at all?

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:34.640
"Picard" Season 2 saw the Borg&nbsp;
Queen manipulating Dr. Agnes Jurati,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:38.240
and the Queen's motives were anything&nbsp;
but noble. Trapped in the 21st century&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:42.800
and imprisoned in one mind, Agnes and&nbsp;
the Queen slowly merged into a single,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.760
sinister new hybrid. Would Agnes become the&nbsp;
first Borg Queen, and birth the cyborg race&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:53.360
in 2024? Would she end up creating the Borg in the&nbsp;
21st century, as Seven of Nine feared? Not quite.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.680
At the urging of Jurati, the Borg Queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:59.920
slowly comes around and the two create&nbsp;
a merged personality with a new goal:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:05.120
to save wayward, dying souls and resurrect&nbsp;
them as a new kind of Borg collective.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:10.480
"With our minds joined as one, we could be more."

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:17.440
The new Borg would be built on cooperation&nbsp;
and salvation, not assimilation. In 2024,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.880
the Jurati Queen takes La Sirena&nbsp;
and leaves for parts unknown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.520
The next time we see her in the&nbsp;
25th century, she has a new,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.640
massive starship and is asking Admiral Picard&nbsp;
about joining the United Federation of Planets.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:30.400
That's all great, but the question remains:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:35.040
What was the Jurati Queen doing for the past&nbsp;
400 years? Are all of the Borg terrors of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.760
past retconned into a separate timeline now? Was&nbsp;
she hiding in a distant part of the galaxy to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:43.680
avoid disrupting the timeline? Did she build&nbsp;
a collective elsewhere? Did she take part in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:49.006
galactic affairs we've never seen? There's now&nbsp;
a 400 year gap that needs a little explaining.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.760
Perhaps the biggest unanswered question of the&nbsp;
bunch closes out the finale. After the combined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.400
efforts of the New Borg and the Federation fleet&nbsp;
prevent a disaster, a unique anomaly is created in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.560
the form of a transwarp conduit. Seven of Nine&nbsp;
recognizes it right away and notes that it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:07.440
unlike any she has seen before, and that's notable&nbsp;
given her lengthy experience with Borg transwarp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:12.240
conduits. Picard wonders who created the conduit,&nbsp;
implying that this was not a natural phenomenon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:16.160
Its creation confounds even the new Borg&nbsp;
Queen, but she knows that it's a threat.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:20.800
It's an ominous closing message, but if there's&nbsp;
one question likely to be resolved in Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.440
it's this one. And it looks like&nbsp;
Picard will need the help of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.840
former Enterprise crew if he's&nbsp;
going to discover the answer:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:30.602
The entire cast of "The Next Generation"&nbsp;
is joining the final season of "Picard."

